Z||000015||mbramble||05-04-2000||09:12 AM||||Wonder if you could go onto e-bay and post a 'fake auction' that had a real Fiero-lover attention getting title and the description of the item is something like "Before bidding on any Fiero items on eBay, you should check out PFF" and also list some web sites of the forum members who have items for sale for reasonable prices.<P>It really astonishes me what some of the items end up going for on ebay.  I bid pretty often but have definite limits on what I will spend for items.  However, almost every item that I have been interested enough to bid on, I have found cheaper on web sites that just sell new or used parts.  I occassionally feel compelled to e-mail a seller to tell them about a particulary bloated price.  For example, a set of dew strips that had a starting bid of $100. He did pull it and I saw one of them listed later with a starting bid of $20.  Much more reasonable.||||reg||1
